Are you tired of working from your kitchen table? Brightwell Commons offers flexible workspace in the heart of Easton's Riverside district. Our members enjoy high-speed Internet, private phone booths, and fully equipped meeting rooms that can be {{135}} online up to two weeks in advance.

Membership plans are available on a daily, monthly, or annual basis. {{136}} members receive a dedicated desk and a personal storage locker, while daily members choose any open seat in our shared lounge. {{137}}

To celebrate our second anniversary, we are offering new members 20 percent off their first three months on any monthly plan. This offer is valid {{138}} April 30. Visit www.brightwellcommons.com/tour to schedule a free visit.

PORT ELLISON (May 4, 2026) — Halvorsen Bakery, known for its rye breads and seasonal pastries, will open its third location on June 15 in the newly redeveloped Wharfside Market. The bakery's owner, Ingrid Halvorsen, said the decision {{139}} by strong demand from customers who had been driving across town to her original shop on Linden Avenue.

The new shop will be considerably larger than the {{140}} two. In addition to a retail counter, it will feature a seating area for 40 guests and a glass-walled kitchen where visitors can watch bakers at work. {{141}}

Ms. Halvorsen plans to hire about 25 employees for the new location. {{142}} interested in applying can find job descriptions on the bakery's Web site. Training for new staff will begin in late May.
